      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Umm. No, I'd like to see it and tell people that the Avatar they found suxx in terms of performance. Most of them have nice animations and look amazing but most I encounter have at least a poor rating. I want to see if that changes over time. From my experience most random people wearing such an avatar never think about the performance or just do not know where to look. So I can at least tell them if the rating is bad. And there are much more people in VRC that just use avatars from a world/cloning  than there are people uploading them. The creators of the avatars get a message about bad performance anyway when they upload. The question is why isn't there a popup in our view when we select an avatar from a world or clone about the performance rating?",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
