  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "With having improved \"Minimum displayed ranking\" system where you are not blocking entire avatar but getting rid of components/objects that are causing performance issues why not hide avatar stats away from public and keep it only to a player using an avatar\n\nMy idea just is about hiding info about the avatar performance stats away from public, and keep it visible only to the person wearing one (For example to look at stats of an avatar from a public world),for the other's they are being controlled by the system anyway, it will also make for a less crowded UI player interaction menu as well as avoiding cases where people would judge someone for having bad ranking.\n\nVRChat should not be about forcing people into optimizing by showing ranking to the other's, let people create stuff they want, new \"Minimum displayed ranking\" allows for creating a lot of nice particle effects and anything else people would want to while not being shown as \"Poor\" or below to everyone, but if people don't want to see their particles both systems \"Safety system\" and \"Minimum displayed performance ranking\" is capable to take care of it.\n\nYou can put all ranking requirements under \"Performance options\" where you change the \"Minimum rank displayed\" option",
